    body: "Thane is governed by its own Thane Municipal Corporation (TMC), one of the largest civic bodies in the country by the population it serves, and it carries its own long-standing nickname - the City of Lakes - built around more than thirty natural and man-made lakes across the city, Masunda Talao (Talao Pali) and Upvan Lake among the best known. That civic weight matters for a career decision: TMC and other local government and public-sector roles are a genuine, visible employment track here in a way no Mumbai-suburb framing captures, and a real share of Thane's population builds a full working life inside the city rather than treating it as a waypoint to Mumbai.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Wagle Estate, Ghodbunder Road, and Kolshet Road are becoming Thane\'s own IT and office-park corridor',
    body: "Wagle Estate began as an industrial estate and is steadily adding IT parks, corporate offices, and business centres alongside its older manufacturing units. Kolshet Road and the stretch of Ghodbunder Road running toward Manpada and Hiranandani Estate now carry a genuine and growing cluster of corporate offices, IT companies, and business parks of their own - not a satellite outpost of a BKC or Powai employer, but a real, if still-maturing, local job market that a growing number of Thane residents can reach without a Mumbai commute at all. For someone choosing a first job or a next move, achieving earlier financial freedom increasingly depends on judging this corridor honestly against a Mumbai-based role, not assuming the better opportunity always sits across the Thane Creek.",
  },
  {
    title: "A genuine pharma and chemical manufacturing belt sits alongside the newer offices",
    body: "Long before Wagle Estate's office towers, the Thane-Belapur Road industrial belt built a real base of pharmaceutical, chemical, and engineering manufacturing units, and that industrial identity has not disappeared - it now runs in parallel with the newer IT and services layer rather than being replaced by it. That gives Thane a genuinely dual local economy: manufacturing, quality, and plant-operations roles on one side, and IT, business-services, and corporate-office roles on the other, both reachable without leaving the city.",
  },
  {
    title: 'A large, family-oriented, Marathi-speaking cultural identity shapes the decision differently than South Mumbai does',
    body: "Thane carries a strong Marathi-speaking cultural core and a settled, multi-generational family character that reads differently from South Mumbai's more transient, cosmopolitan pace - many households here have built their lives across two or three generations in the same neighbourhood. That texture matters for career counselling: family expectation, local reputation, and a preference for stability often carry more weight in a Thane household's career conversation than in a purely transplant-heavy Mumbai suburb, and good guidance should recognise that instead of applying a one-size-fits-all metro framing.",
  },
];

const commuteVsLocalItems = [
